WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.701
-Hey, bud!

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.336
Oh, it's so good to see ya,

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:06.639
and thank you for doing the
TikTok dance challenge with me.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:09.576
-I was honored. I was honored.
Thank you.

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:11.544
-I haven't seen you in a while
on the show

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:14.279
because you took a break
from acting.

00:00:14.279 --> 00:00:16.482
And you're now a dad.

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:17.650
-Exactly, man. Yeah.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.853
I feel lucky I got to
take some time off,

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:24.657
and I have two boys, and it's --
it's the best, man, the best.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.826
-Look at that.
Look at the smile.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.562
-I know. It's so true.
-It's the greatest thing.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:32.031
I'm so happy because
you're just a perfect --

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:34.500
I always saw you being a dad,
so I think it's great.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.869
-Thanks, man. That's one of
the sweetest things

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:38.037
you could say about a person.

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:40.840
I saw you in that documentary
about dads

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.377
that Bryce Dallas Howard made
about dads,

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.713
and I was -- I've been wanting
to tell you this

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.514
ever since I saw it.
I saw it a few weeks ago.

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:51.684
And you were --
you were saying like --

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.152
The question was
"What is a dad?"

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:55.555
And you were like, "A dad is"

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:56.589
and you were looking for
the right word,

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.357
and you were like, "a hero."

00:00:58.357 --> 00:01:02.228
And I just about started crying
when you said that, man.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.996
-I was like, "I said that?"

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:08.100
-Thinking about, like,
what you --

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.604
I'm someone's dad now, 'cause I
remember looking up to my dad

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:14.206
that exact same way, and just --
-Yeah.

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:16.676
-You know, there's not really
a lot of other people

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:19.512
you can just grab them
and be like, "Ohh."

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.480
-[ Laughs ]
-You know what I mean?

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.482
-Yeah, exactly right.

00:01:23.482 --> 00:01:25.418
And I think there probably
will come a certain age

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.820
where it's not that easy to get
them and do that, you know?

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.855
-Yeah, you're probably right.
Right now I still can.

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:31.357
-Yeah, I know, me too.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:35.995
You know, "HitRecord," I always
loved that you created this

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:40.466
before, like, there was any kind
of collab going on the Internet.

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:42.468
It was way ahead of its time,

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:44.903
and I love that you made that,
and I still check it out.

00:01:44.903 --> 00:01:47.740
-Dude, you've been a supporter
of it for the whole time.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.942
You were an early,
early champion

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:51.343
of the whole "HitRecord"
community.

00:01:51.343 --> 00:01:56.015
-It's created so many awesome,
fun, creative things.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:59.686
And on the site,
it has some creative prompts

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:02.989
for people to see, and just see
how that can inspire something.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.658
And I thought it would be kind
of fun if maybe you could answer

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:08.027
some of the prompts that we've
gotten from the website

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.496
and just see what maybe
your answer would be.

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:11.631
-Yeah, sure, sure.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:12.898
-These are tricky, by the way.

00:02:12.898 --> 00:02:15.435
These are great questions.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:17.937
You can only bring one album
to a deserted island

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:21.073
and have to listen to it on loop
for the rest of your life.

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:23.409
What are you picking?

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.945
-I mean, listen to any album
on loop the rest of your life,

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:27.247
that's hard, but --
-It is tricky.

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:30.616
-It's probably "The Point!"
by Harry Nilsson.

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:31.917
-What?!

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:33.018
-Do you know that record?

00:02:33.018 --> 00:02:34.154
-I love -- I was gonna say

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.921
"Nilsson Schmilsson,"
Harry Nilsson.

00:02:35.921 --> 00:02:37.389
-Are you kidding? Really?

00:02:37.389 --> 00:02:40.359
-Really, I swear, and we didn't
talk before this.

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:43.796
But "The Point!" --
"Me and My Arrow."

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:47.266
-Yeah, exactly.
-"Think About Your Troubles."

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.469
Alright, this one blew my mind.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:50.703
I would love to know
your answer.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.273
Look at this photo, please.

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:56.876
What is this astronaut thinking?

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.478
-She's got her, like, helmet on,

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.279
so she can't breathe
the air anymore.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:01.514
I'm going dark with this.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:02.815
She can't breathe the air
anymore.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.217
The air's not healthy to
breathe. She can't go outside.

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:07.586
She's trying to write down
her memoir, and she hates it.

00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:09.255
So she's throwing it
on the ground.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:12.225
-I think this picture was taken
last week and she was like,

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:14.159
"When is the new season of
'Ozark'?"

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:16.729
[ Laughter ]
"Let's go. I need something.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:19.632
Let's go."

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:22.201
I want to talk about your movie.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:23.803
I saw it.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.438
We had Jamie Foxx on the show.

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:27.373
It's called "Project Power."

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:32.078
Basically the idea is
there might be a new drug

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:35.248
on the planet or a pill that you
take and you become the most --

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.883
you have secret superpowers
for five minutes.

00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:40.653
-Mm-hmm, yeah, and you don't
know what you're gonna get.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.722
The pill might give you
something good.

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.989
It's different for everybody.

00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:46.292
It might give you something bad.
Might kill you.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.194
It's an entertaining premise.

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.996
-It's a great premise
for a movie.

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:52.465
And I love Dominique Fishback.

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.100
I've never seen her before.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.601
-Yes!
-She was fantastic.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:56.669
-I'm really happy
you brought her up.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.170
She's my favorite part
of this movie.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.105
And I'm a huge Jamie Foxx fan.

00:04:00.105 --> 00:04:03.008
Loved him ever since
"In Living Color," everything.

00:04:03.008 --> 00:04:05.611
But Dominique Fishback --
Anybody out there who loves

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:09.014
movies, actors, acting,
just a fan of seeing

00:04:09.014 --> 00:04:12.718
an up-and-coming new, brilliant
talent -- Dominique Fishback.

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:15.855
I'm so happy to be
her collaborator, her friend.

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.323
She's so good.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:20.359
-Jamie Foxx --
For me, he can do no wrong.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:22.662
Both of you guys together.
I'm like --

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:25.130
I heard that he comes --
When he does a movie,

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.533
he has entrance music on a set.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.368
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:31.737
He d-- That's true, actually.
-I've never heard of that.

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:34.974
-He does. I mean, I listen to
music on set a lot too.

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:37.877
It's useful when you're trying
to act and concentrate.

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:39.478
I put in headphones, though.

00:04:39.478 --> 00:04:41.347
Jamie doesn't come
with headphones.

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:44.183
Jamie comes to set
with a backpack

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:48.788
with a built-in massive speaker
just bumping his music,

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:51.256
whatever he's playing, and he
plays a wide variety of music.

00:04:51.256 --> 00:04:54.727
But it's actually really cool
because he's bringing everybody

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:57.463
into his creative process.
You know what I mean?

00:04:57.463 --> 00:05:00.299
Like, instead of being like,
"I'm focused, don't talk to me,"

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:03.068
he's like, "Everybody on
the crew feel this with me."

00:05:03.068 --> 00:05:05.003
And it really livens
everybody up.

00:05:05.003 --> 00:05:06.606
Jamie is brilliant. I love him.

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:09.075
-I got to get one of those
backpacks, like a boompack.

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:11.277
-I know.
-And just like, yeah.

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:13.312
And just come in --
-He pulls it off really well.

00:05:13.312 --> 00:05:16.315
It might play
a little differently on you.

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:18.384
I'm just saying.
Like, I love you, Jimmy.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:20.085
It might play --
[ Laughs ]

00:05:20.085 --> 00:05:22.454
-No, but I'll be walking in,
playing Harry Nilsson,

00:05:22.454 --> 00:05:26.091
cranking it up.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:27.560
-Well, I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.562
Here's Joseph Gordon-Levitt
in "Project Power."

00:05:30.562 --> 00:05:32.164
Take a look at this on Netflix.

00:05:32.164 --> 00:05:34.167
-On your knees,
hands behind your head.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:35.634
NOPD.

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.236
Ah, I see we have a lady
here as well.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.505
You too, ma'am.
Hands, very good.

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:40.606
Thank you.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:43.776
Now, how's everybody
doing tonight?

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:46.578
You sure you want to do that,
young man?

00:05:46.578 --> 00:05:48.881
You ever taken
one of those before?

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.517
You haven't, had you?
I can tell.

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:54.387
Now, I bet you heard it can make
you fast, make you strong.

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:55.687
Make this a fair fight,

00:05:55.687 --> 00:05:57.322
even though I got a gun
pointed at your face.

00:05:57.322 --> 00:06:00.225
-Just twist it, Tommy.

00:06:00.225 --> 00:06:02.227
-But that's only if you happen
to have a good power.

00:06:02.227 --> 00:06:03.529
Not everybody does.

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.331
Some people take it
and just blow up.

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:06.699
-I don't want to do this
anymore, man.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:07.800
-Shut up.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.837
-So the question is,
what's your power?

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:12.304
Might be good, might be bad.

00:06:12.304 --> 00:06:13.305
Nobody knows.

00:06:13.305 --> 00:06:14.574
-Take the pill, Tommy.

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:15.908
-Take it.

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:17.977
Go ahead.

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:20.445
I want to see what happens.

00:06:20.445 --> 00:06:22.081
-Joseph Gordon-Levitt,

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:24.483
hopefully we get to see
each other in person soon.

00:06:24.483 --> 00:06:28.121
"Project Power" begins streaming
this Friday on Netflix.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:30.856
Hug that family, buddy.
I love you.

00:06:30.856 --> 00:06:32.392
-I will, man. Thank you.
-Great to see you.

